Preconditions:
[PRE:CLEAR_SESSION]
Anonymous shopper. {{FRONT_URL}} accessible. B2B-store must be at its default barcode settings (scannerEnabled=true, fields=[]) for this case — Steps force that state before observing, since it cannot rely on another case's Cleanup having run first.
@td(BARCODE_FULLTEXT_DISCRIM.sku) carries the GTIN as its own gtin field; @td(BARCODE_FULLTEXT_DISCRIM.otherSku) carries the same value as a whole word in its NAME — full-text must find both, exact would find only the first.

Assertions:
[MATH] product count for ?q={{code}} >= 2 (matches @td(BARCODE_FULLTEXT_DISCRIM.sku) by GTIN and @td(BARCODE_FULLTEXT_DISCRIM.otherSku) by name) {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the 'Search' input displays {{code}} as the active phrase under ?q= — full-text is unchanged by this feature {SPEC}
[REL] the ?barcode={{code}} request on this same unconfigured store returns a DIFFERENT, smaller result than the ?q={{code}} request on the same store — the literal 'barcode' index field matches neither seeded product {SPEC}
[DOM] the ?barcode= page shows a visible, intact result (empty state or a short list) — never a crash or blank grid {BL}

